cmd-persistentinv_panel-desc = Opens the persistent inventory administration panel.
cmd-persistentinv_panel-help = Usage: persistentinv_panel [player|UserId]
persistentinv-admin-title = Persistent inventory
persistentinv-admin-players = Players
persistentinv-admin-target = Player name or account UUID, including offline players
persistentinv-admin-load = Find
persistentinv-admin-refresh = Refresh
persistentinv-admin-select-player = Select a player to inspect their persistent inventory.
persistentinv-admin-overview = State and diagnostics
persistentinv-admin-snapshots = Snapshots and items
persistentinv-admin-history = Operation history
persistentinv-admin-actions = Management
persistentinv-admin-item-search = Filter by prototype, item number or container…
persistentinv-admin-history-search = Filter by action, administrator, reason or snapshot…
persistentinv-admin-history-limit = Latest 100 operations. All times are UTC.
persistentinv-admin-actions-hint = Actions apply to the player shown above. Enter a reason and confirm the button.
persistentinv-admin-reason = Required reason, up to 512 characters
persistentinv-admin-force = Force saving a restrained character
persistentinv-admin-save = Save character
persistentinv-admin-invalidate = Invalidate snapshot
persistentinv-admin-quarantine = Quarantine
persistentinv-admin-rollback = Roll back to selected snapshot
persistentinv-admin-recover = Recover last disconnect loss
persistentinv-admin-save-hint = Save: stores the current inventory, removes the body and returns the player to the lobby.
persistentinv-admin-invalidate-hint = Invalidate: disables restoration of the snapshot; world items are preserved.
persistentinv-admin-quarantine-hint = Quarantine: blocks restoration without issuing or deleting items.
persistentinv-admin-rollback-hint = Rollback uses the snapshot selected in “Snapshots and items”; recover uses the last disconnect loss.
persistentinv-admin-validate = Validate selected snapshot
persistentinv-admin-reload-cache = Reload account cache
persistentinv-admin-open-logs = Player inventory logs
persistentinv-admin-legacy-resources = This legacy snapshot has no saved resource state. Unknown ammunition and gas will restore empty; saved physical items will be retained.
persistentinv-admin-busy = Request in progress…
persistentinv-admin-player-missing = Player not found.
persistentinv-admin-snapshot-missing = This snapshot is no longer available for the selected account.
persistentinv-admin-no-snapshot = This account has no persistent inventory record.
persistentinv-admin-no-items = No items match the filter.
persistentinv-admin-offline = The player has no active character session.
persistentinv-admin-error = Request failed: { $error }. See the server log for details.
persistentinv-admin-stale = Account state changed. Data refreshed; review it before repeating the action.
persistentinv-admin-target-busy = A save, transfer, reset or life transition is still running. Refresh after it completes.
persistentinv-admin-reason-required = Enter a non-empty reason of no more than 512 characters.
persistentinv-admin-validation-ok = Isolated snapshot restoration and canonical verification succeeded. No items were issued.
persistentinv-admin-validation-failed = Snapshot validation failed: { $error }
persistentinv-admin-cache-reloaded = Account cache reloaded from the database.
persistentinv-admin-payload-ok = Payload size, structure and SHA256 verified. Inspect migrations below; full restoration can be checked separately.
persistentinv-admin-details-truncated = Display limit reached. The stored snapshot has not been modified.
persistentinv-storage-snapshot-too-large = Inventory exceeds the 128 KiB save limit. Your items remain with you. Reduce the contents and try again.
persistentinv-storage-quota-exceeded = Your persistent inventory storage quota is full. Your items remain with you. Contact an administrator.
persistentinv-storage-usage = Account storage estimate: { $bytes } / { $limit } bytes (excluding database overhead).
    Payload: { $payload } bytes; snapshots: { $snapshots }; unique payloads: { $blobs }.
    History: { $events } events / { $history } bytes; operation receipts: { $receipts }.
    Totals: saves { $saves }, losses { $losses }, recoveries { $recoveries }.
persistentinv-storage-total = System: { $accounts } accounts, { $bytes } payload bytes. Legacy accounts over the new limits: { $over }.
persistentinv-storage-history = Detailed history: up to 100 events / 64 KiB / 14 days. Removed events: { $pruned }. Operation safety records are retained separately.
